From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:02:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Move to PostgreSQL

Move from SQLite to PostgreSQL. Where the original took SQLite and
PostgreSQL both, with branches on the dialect in its code, this one
changes the database. A project writes and checks its migrations in one
dialect only.

- Make an empty database on the server (createdb board) and change the
  address in .env. .env is not committed, so the patch does not have it:

      MAAGO_DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost:5432/board

- The driver becomes pgx. Change one import each in main.go and
  board/board_test.go to github.com/jackc/pgx/v5/stdlib, and go mod tidy
  adds pgx to go.mod and drops modernc.org/sqlite
- Migrations belong to a dialect. Delete the four of SQLite (0001 to
  0004), and maago makemigrations writes a new first draft for
  PostgreSQL, 0001_initial.sql. The data does not move: start on a new
  database
- The models, queries, views, templates and tests stay as they are. No
  query has SQL of one dialect only, and maago gen checks the queries
  again on a PostgreSQL practice database

    maago migrate
    go test ./...

maagotest.DB(t) in the tests reads the .env at the root too, and makes
a schema for each test on that server.

Maago-Database: postgres

